        acquisition = "Difficulty: Easy - A purchasable scouting-map toy provides a shortcut; manual exploration is also available.\n\n1. Choose the scouting-map shortcut or the exploration route. First check your Toy Box for the Eastern Kingdoms scouting map; an already learned copy can be used again without buying another.\n\n2. For the shortcut, Alliance buy Scouting Map: Modern Provisioning of the Eastern Kingdoms from Krom Stoutarm in Ironforge (74.6,9.8). Horde buy Scouting Map: The Eastern Kingdoms Campaign from Estelle Gendry atop Orgrimmar's main gate (56.8,89.8). The base price is 10,000 gold; it does not require already earning this exploration meta.\n\n3. Learn and USE the toy on your character, then check Eastern Kingdoms Explorer and its zone criteria. The current map grants exploration as well as flight paths; older comments saying it teaches only a few flight paths predate the update. Finish any criterion still missing rather than buying the wrong continent's map.\n\n4. For manual exploration, track each missing zone achievement and use its detailed route. Southern circuit: Elwynn -> Westfall -> Duskwood -> Northern Stranglethorn -> the Cape -> Deadwind Pass -> Swamp of Sorrows -> Blasted Lands. Use Zidormi at Blasted Lands 48.2,7.2 for its pre-invasion phase.\n\n5. Northern circuit: Tirisfal -> Silverpine -> Hillsbrad -> Arathi -> Hinterlands -> Western Plaguelands -> Eastern Plaguelands, plus Ghostlands, Eversong Woods (Burning Crusade) and Isle of Quel'Danas. Use Zidormi at Tirisfal 69.5,62.8 for pre-battle Lordaeron. After Midnight, enter the old Ghostlands portal beside Zidormi at Eastern Plaguelands 53.8,8.6; Horde can also use Orgrimmar's downstairs Silvermoon (Burning Crusade) portal. For old Quel'Danas, use Shattrath's portal behind Exarch Nasuun at 49.0,42.3. The new Midnight Eversong achievement is separate.\n\n6. Central circuit: Wetlands -> Loch Modan -> Dun Morogh -> Badlands -> Searing Gorge -> Burning Steppes -> Redridge. Recheck the 