            "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=714#comments:id=2865317",
        },
        tips = "The three reputations are still obtainable. Removed battleground marks, old guild reputation perks and historical exact match-count estimates are not required.",
        reviewedAt = "2026-11-03",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=714",
        areaMaps = { 91, 1366, 1339 },
        difficultyReason = "Exalted battleground reputation requires a substantial number of objective-focused matches.",
        difficulty = "hard",
    },
    [728] = {
        name = "Explore Durotar",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Easy - Follow the zone discovery pins; no rare drop or organized group is required.\n\n1. Track Explore Durotar and check which named areas are still missing. Use the Durotar map for these coordinates. Fly or ride through each missing area's discovery boundary; a fully visible map alone is not proof that every criterion credited.\n\n2. Southern coast and starting valley: Valley of Trials (44.2, 64.7) -> Northwatch Foothold (49.8, 81.5) -> Sen'jin Village (56.0, 74.4) -> Echo Isles (64.1, 74.4) -> Tiragarde Keep (59.5, 58.3).\n\n3. Cross the middle of the zone: Razormane Grounds (49.1, 48.8) -> Southfury Watershed (43.1, 42.5) -> Razor Hill (52.8, 42.8).\n\n4. Finish the northern ravines and city boundary: Thunder Ridge (40.9, 26.5) -> Drygulch Ravine (52.6, 21.5) -> Skull Rock (55.0, 10.0) -> Orgrimmar boundary (53.0, 1.0).\n\n5. Reopen the achievement and check every named criterion. If one is missing, return to its pin and move around the actual subzone, descending toward the ground if necessary. Stop once the discovery credits; extra map shading and nearby dungeons are not additional requirements.",
        source = "Explore Durotar",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        sourceURL = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=728#comments",
        achievementId = 728,
        category = "Exploration",
        stepCount = 5,
        waypoints = {
            { mapID = 1, x = 0.44170000000000004, y = 0.6468, step = 2, label = "Valley of Trials" },
            { mapID = 1, x = 0.4982, y = 0.815, step = 2, label = "Northwatch Foothold" },
            { mapID = 1, x = 0.5598, y = 0.7436, step = 2, label = "Sen'jin Village" },
            { mapID = 1, x = 0.6414, y = 0.7441, step = 2, label = "Echo Isles" },
            { mapID = 1, x = 0.5951, y = 0.583, step = 2, label = "Tiragarde Keep" },
            { mapID = 1, x = 0.4911, y = 0.48810000000000003, step = 3, label = "Razormane Grounds" },
            { mapID = 1, x = 0.4315, y = 0.4255, step = 3, label = "Southfury Watershed" },
            { mapID = 1, x = 0.5283, y = 0.42810000000000004, step = 3, label = "Razor Hill" },
            { mapID = 1, x = 0.409, y = 0.2651, step = 4, label = "Thunder Ridge" },
            { mapID = 1, x = 0.526, y = 0.2152, step = 4, label = "Drygulch Ravine" },
            { mapID = 1, x = 0.5497, y = 0.09960000000000001, step = 4, label = "Skull Rock" },
            { mapID = 1, x = 0.53, y = 0.01, step = 4, label = "Orgrimmar boundary" },
        },
        sources = {
            "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=728#comments:id=1297419",
            "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=728#comments:id=1485985",
            "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=728#comments:id=2006732",
            "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=728#comments:id=5660777",
        },
        tips = "Razormane Grounds moved relative to old maps; do not use the old 41,45 pin. Alliance can approach the Orgrimmar boundary from the north/Azshara side, flying into its discovery area and checking credit before going deeper among guards. For Valley of Trials, a 2023 comment uses the southern slope near 49.5,70.5 to avoid its guarded entrance.",
        reviewedAt = "2026-11-03",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=728",
        difficultyReason = "Follow the zone discovery pins; no rare drop or organized group is required.",
        difficulty = "easy",
    },
    [729] = {
        name = "Deathcharger's Reins",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Rare drops or scarce Black Market auctions make the acquisition unpredictable.\n\nDifficulty: Hard - The final Stratholme boss has a low mount drop chance, so many repeat runs may be needed.\n\n1. Set dungeon difficulty to Normal and enter Stratholme through the SERVICE ENTRANCE / Eastwall Gate in Eastern Plaguelands (43.3, 19.7). Check the dungeon map: you want Service Entrance / the Gauntlet. If it loads Main Gate, leave, reset all instances, then re-enter through the service gate.\n\n2. Kill Baroness Anastari, Nerub'enkan and Maleki the Pallid at the three ziggurats. After each boss, enter its ziggurat and kill every Thuzadin Acolyte inside. All three crystals must be disabled to open the way to Slaughter Square.\n\n3. Enter Slaughter Square and kill all the abominations. Kill Ramstein the Gorger when he emerges, then finish the undead wave and Black Guard Sentries so the Slaughterhouse opens.\n\n4. Kill Lord Aurius Rivendare inside and loot him for a chance at Deathcharger's Reins. The drop is random; kill order, crates and speed do not guarantee it. The old Baron name in comments refers to this same mount farm.\n\n5. If the reins did not drop, return outside the instance, choose Reset All Instances on your portrait and run it again. Pause at the hourly instance limit. Old Dreamwalk/follower-dungeon exit tricks have had graveyard bugs; walking out is the dependable route.\n\n6. When the reins drop, use them to learn Rivendare's Deathcharger. Either faction can learn and ride it.\n\n7. After learning the exact mount, check Deathcharger's Reins in Achievements. A similarly named mount or merely killing the former drop boss does not satisfy this record.",
        source = "Lord Aurius Rivendare - Normal Stratholme, Service Entrance",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        sourceURL = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=729#comments",
        achievementId = 729,
        category = "Collections",
        stepCount = 7,
        waypoints = {
