    [2336] = {
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Combine several long reputation grinds, rogue-farmed junkboxes and monthly Faire access.\n\n1. Choose ONE character and use it for every required standing: Honored Bloodsail Buccaneers, plus Exalted Booty Bay, Ratchet, Gadgetzan, Everlook, Ravenholdt and Darkmoon Faire. The earned title is account-wide, but earning different required reputations on different alts does not complete this achievement. Shen'dralar and Syndicate reputation are not requirements.\n\n2. Start Darkmoon Faire alongside the other grinds whenever it is open; check its in-game calendar week each month. On Darkmoon Island, buy a Ride Ticket Book from Kae Ti around 50.4,59.0, open it, and ride the adjacent carousel until WHEE! reaches 60 minutes. Refresh this 10% reputation buff before large quest/junkbox turn-ins. The Top Hat is an alternative, not a second stacking Faire buff. A Battle Standard of Coordination helps nearby kill reputation if your guild has unlocked it.\n\n3. For Bloodsail, enable At War with Booty Bay and kill its Bruisers around the docks/tavern (Cape 42,74) until HONORED. Stay in normal Booty Bay rather than starting the old under-siege quest chain. Attacking a town NPC can call guards; rotate between nearby spots when reinforcements stop. This damages all four goblin reputations, so do it before restoring them.\n\n4. While Bloodsail is friendly and Booty Bay hated, complete Avast Ye, Admiral! from Fleet Master Firallon below decks on the middle Wild Shore ship (46.6,95.2). Kill Revilgaz and Seahorn on the tavern roof balcony (41.0,73.0), then turn in to Firallon. Friendly is enough for that quest, but verify HONORED Bloodsail for Insane before leaving this grind. Doing the hat quest now also avoids the old-credit problems reported by returning players.\n\n5. Choose how to restore the goblins. To KEEP Bloodsail Honored, skip the cloth quests and farm the pirates in the next step directly, even while hated by the towns. Alternatively, after recording Honored Bloodsail and finishing the hat quest, the repeatable cloth quests below can repair goblin access faster but LOWER Bloodsail. You do not need both opposing standings simultaneously; this choice determines which reputations you keep afterward.\n\n6. Optional cloth repair ONLY if you accept losing Bloodsail: Mupsi Shacklefridd west of Ratchet (Northern Barrens 65.8,72.0) takes 40 Linen Cloth + 4 Crystal Vials; Bronn Fitzwrench outside Everlook (Winterspring 58.0,52.2) takes 40 Runecloth + 4 Coal; the Bloodsail Traitor north of Booty Bay (Cape 48.5,63.3) takes 40 Silk Cloth + 4 Red Dye; Rumsen Fizzlebrack outside Gadgetzan (Tanaris 50.4,27.2) takes 40 Mageweave Cloth + 4 Strong Flux. Each hand-in gives 500 base reputation to its city and 250 spillover to each of the other three. The city's quest stops at Neutral. Prioritize Everlook/Ratchet before Gadgetzan, check all four standings, and buy more materials only while an available repair quest is still needed.\n\n7. Farm Southsea pirates at Lost Rigger Cove behind the Caverns of Time in Tanaris. Cover the northern camp around 72.3,47.4 and southern shore camp around 69,54, including their nearby ships as needed. A PARTY of up to five can split the camps and encourage faster respawns; do not convert it to a raid, which current reports say stops sharing the kills' reputation. Stay within your guild banner's range if using one. These pirates restore the goblins without lowering Bloodsail.\n\n8. Continue until Booty Bay, Ratchet AND Everlook reach Exalted; Gadgetzan usually gets there first but stops at 20,999/21,000 Revered. Then kill a pirate at Fray Island (Northern Barrens 77,90) to supply Gadgetzan's final point through spillover. Check each of the FOUR named cities rather than stopping at the Steamwheedle heading or at Revered. No fixed kill count applies to every starting standing and buff combination.\n\n9. For Ravenholdt's kill phase, use BFA-era Arathi Highlands. If needed, speak to Zidormi near the southern bridge (38.2,90.0) and select that era, not the newer TWW story phase. Find the Syndicate at Dabyrie's Farmstead around 50,41 or Go'shek Farm around 51.7,60.1, depending on the current Warfront control. Kill the Syndicate humanoids and Harvest Shredders, check that they give Ravenholdt reputation, and circle the active farm with a small party until 11,999/12,000 HONORED. This is one point BEFORE Revered; do not keep killing after the cap.\n\n10. Arrange Heavy Junkboxes with a rogue alt or another rogue; your achievement character can be any class. One proven route is CURRENT Lower Blackrock Spire: enter the upper-balcony portal inside Blackrock Mountain (80.5,40.7 on its upper map), then stealth through the lower dungeon and pickpocket humanoids before killing them. Reverse the route once pockets have replenished, or leave/reset when appropriate. This uses LBRS, not the Warlords Upper Blackrock Spire instance.\n\n11. An outdoor lockbox alternative is Greengill Coast on the OLD Isle of Quel'Danas. After Midnight, use the Isle of Quel'Danas portal in Shattrath to reach this Burning Crusade zone. Pickpocket the Greengill Slave camps around 63,54 and 64,48, THEN kill them and move between the camps as they respawn. Empty bags beforehand and mail/deposit the boxes regularly. A rogue is needed for Pick Pocket; other classes should arrange boxes from one rather than merely killing murlocs.\n\n12. Bring the Heavy Junkboxes to Winstone Wolfe INSIDE Ravenholdt Manor, ground floor on the left (Hillsbrad 71.4,45.0). Use Junkboxes Needed: five boxes give 75 base Ravenholdt reputation. From the exact 11,999/12,000 Honored kill cap, the unbuffed requirement is 1,405 boxes; active quest-reputation buffs reduce it. Save turn-ins for WHEE! if convenient. Keep the boxes unopened, use mail/Warband bank for storage, and leave bag space for quest rewards. Wolfe handles the current turn-in, not Fahrad upstairs.\n\n13. For Darkmoon Faire Exalted, return during each Faire week and do the daily minigames/races, the monthly quests for your professions, and the nine Darkmoon artifact quests. Get a Darkmoon Adventurer's Guide from Selina Dourman near the entrance so relevant dungeon/PvP artifacts can drop, or buy the specific quest items from other players. Turn them in on the SAME achievement character with WHEE! active. Pet-battle dailies do not replace these reputation quests.\n\n14. To speed Darkmoon reputation with gold, assemble full traditional Darkmoon decks whose turn-in quest explicitly rewards Darkmoon Faire reputation, then repeat those hand-ins. Check the actual deck/quest before buying: a modern Darkmoon trinket is not automatically a reputation turn-in. Otherwise continue the monthly and daily activities until Exalted. Do not discard a primary profession merely to add another profession quest.\n\n15. When the final required standing is reached, check the achievement and title. If it does not award, verify all seven standings were earned on THIS character and relog once before redoing anything. The Bloodsail Admiral achievement by itself proves only Friendly, not necessarily Honored. Do not destroy Exalted goblin standings to repeat Bloodsail solely because an old tracker displays it unchecked; current completions and replies confirm the route still works in Retail.",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Insane in the Membrane",
        sourceURL = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=2336#comments",
